[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - A is perturbed, so A:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - B is not a descendant of A (since B is an upstream node), so B:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - C is not a descendant of A (C is a descendant of B), so C:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - D is not a descendant of A (D is a descendant of B), so D:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - This matches the observation.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 2. **Perturb(B) -> A:0, B:0, C:0, D:1**  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - B is perturbed, so B:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - A is a descendant of B (B -> C -> A), so A:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - C is a descendant of B (B -> C), so C:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - D is a descendant of B (B -> D), so D:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - This matches the observation.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 3. **Perturb(C) -> A:1, B:1, C:0, D:1**  
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - C is perturbed, so C:0.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - A is a descendant of C (C -> A), so A:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - B is a descendant of C (C -> D -> B), so B:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - D is a descendant of C (C -> D), so D:1.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m    - This matches the observation.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m All three perturbation observations are consistent with the candidate graph.
