[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m #### **Perturb(B) -> A:1, B:0, C:0, D:1**
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - A is a descendant of B (since B->A).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - D is not a descendant of B (since there is no edge from B to D).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - C is not a descendant of B or D (no edges from B or D to C).
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - Hence, perturbing B causes:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - A:1 (B is upstream, so B is 1, A is a downstream of B)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - B:0 (B is perturbed, so it is 0)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - C:0 (C is not a descendant of B or D)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - D:0 (D is not a descendant of B or D)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m **Observation**: A:1, B:0, C:0, D:0 → but the perturbation observation says A:1, B:0, C:0, D:1. This is **inconsistent**.
