[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - C: downstream of B
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - D: not downstream of B
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - Therefore:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - A:0, B:0, C:1, D:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - **Perturb(B) -> A:0 B:0 C:1 D:0** ✅ Consistent with the observation.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m **Case 3: Perturb(D)** (D is perturbed, others are not)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - Node D is 0 (as it is the perturbed node)
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - For other nodes (A, B, C):
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - A has an incoming edge from D (D → A)? No, D → B and D → C, not A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - B has an incoming edge from D (D → B), so B is a downstream of D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - C has an incoming edge from D (D → C), so C is a downstream of D.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - A: no path from D to A.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - Therefore:
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m   - A:0, B:1, C:1, D:0
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m - **Perturb(D) -> A:1 B:1 C:1 D:0** ✅ Consistent with the observation.
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m ---
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m 
[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=2716495)[0m **Conclusion**: All three perturbation observations are consistent with the candidate graph.
